# Everything the image does not need. Kept deliberately explicit rather than
# broad, because a `.dockerignore` that is too generous produces an image that
# builds and then fails at runtime, and one that is too tight ships the whole
# development toolchain to production.

# Build output and dependencies: the image gets these from the build stage, not
# from the host, and copying a host `node_modules` is how Windows and Linux
# binaries end up mixed.
.next
node_modules

# VCS and CI
.git
.github

# Tests and their tooling. Not in the runtime, and `test/e2e` pulls Playwright.
test
coverage
playwright.config.ts
playwright-report
test-results

# Local environment. A `.env.local` on a developer machine is the single most
# dangerous thing to bake into an image, and the build stage must not read it.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Developer scratch
test-results
.vscode
.idea
AGENTWORK.md

# Docs and the agent coordination files: none of it is served.
docs
README.md
ROADMAP.md
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
